  "scope": "The original primitive cusp form of weight at least two and prime p greater than three constructs the genuine local coefficient extension and continuous two-dimensional representation with exact original Fourier and weight norm-Frobenius values, actual odd complex conjugation, and trivial action of every original norm-inertia subgroup outside Q*p. Finite trace invariance, complete trace invariance, faithful trace-algebra kernel detection and both matrix-kernel preservation branches are proved. No matrix, trace or inertia certificate is supplied. Full original association, the remaining local/image/regularity inputs, exceptional-prime scope, automorphy and literal higher symmetric-power continuation remain unresolved. The existing absolute arithmetic-descent lemma has a discrete target and cannot be applied directly to these local-field matrices. Review the existing adic matrix and stable-lattice descent results before expanding that dependency. Acceptance remains16/20 and DUB-17--20 OPEN; full scratch and subsequent assembled verification are still required."
